-- 하경수 교수 회신 반영 (2026-11-17, 워드·영문으로 받음, 국문은 번역). 받은 항목만 바꾸고 나머지 칸은 그대로 둔다. 사진은 관리자 화면에서 올린다.

update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서울대학교 화학공학 1995 공학사</li><li>서울대학교 화학공학 1997 공학석사</li><li>서울대학교 화학공학 2001 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>LG화학 기술연구원 팀장·선임연구원 (2001–2009)</li><li>한국화학연구원(KRICT) 책임연구원 (2009–2014)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 교수 (2014–현재)</li><li>서강대학교 C1 가스 리파이너리 사업단 연구그룹장 (2017–2024)</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>Chinese Journal of Catalysis 객원편집위원 (2023–2024)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Mansoor Ali, Muhammad Kashif Khan, Muhammad Zubair, Faisal Zafar, Sheraz Ahmed, Muhammad Asif, Ahmed Haleley, Zaman Sajid, Jong Wook Bae*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Integrated Framework for Electrochemical N₂ Reduction to NH₃: Mechanistic Pathways, Theoretical Descriptors, and Data-Driven Catalyst Design," <em>Carbon Energy</em> (2026), accepted</li><li>Seojin Shin, Kyeongjun Seo, Seung-Jun Baek, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Wangyun Won*, "Ethylene production from shale gas using a dielectric barrier discharge plasma reactor: an integrative circular economy perspective," <em>Green Chemistry</em> 28, 11764–11778 (2026) – Front Cover <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/d5gc07016c">doi.org/10.1039/d5gc07016c</a></li><li>Minkyeong Ban, Juchan Kim, Hyeonae Im, Seongseop Kim, Hoang Phuong Nguyen, Yongju Yun, Jeong Woo Han*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Jinwoo Lee*, "Light oils from methane homologation over hierarchically porous TiO₂/SiO₂ hybrid catalyst for a non-thermal plasma," <em>Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy</em> 386, 126437 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126437">doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126437</a></li><li>Hyeonae Im, Hoang Phuong Nguyen, Yunkyung Kim, Juchan Kim, Chaesung Lim, Yongju Yun, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Jeong Woo Han*, "Computationally guided dopant discovery for boosting TiO₂ catalysts in plasma-assisted non-oxidative coupling of methane," <em>Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy</em> 383, 126051 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2025.126051">doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2025.126051</a></li><li>Dong Hyeon Kim, Hee Hwan Kim, Juchan Kim, Youngchang Byun*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Recovery of methyl methacrylate from waste poly(methyl methacrylate) pellets using a low-temperature plasma and zeolites," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 497, 154438 (2024) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.154438">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.154438</a></li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Ethylene Production Processes in a Carbon-Neutral Strategy," <em>Energy Conversion and Management</em> 311, 118462 (2024) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.enconman.2024.118462">doi.org/10.1016/j.enconman.2024.118462</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Seongseop Kim, Minkyeong Ban, Dongmin Lee, Seongbeen Kim, Jinwoo Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Unravelling the effects of short pore on Fischer-Tropsch synthesis and its role as selectivity controller," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 475, 146039 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.146039">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.146039</a></li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "A Combined Production Technology for Ethylene and Hydrogen with an Ethane Cracking Center and Dielectric Barrier Discharge Plasma Reactor," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 462, 142155 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.142155">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.142155</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Chaesung Lim, Dongmin Lee, Hayoung Jeong, Jeong Woo Han*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Effects of oxygen species in perovskite catalysts on the partial oxidation of methane in a low temperature plasma bed," <em>Journal of Catalysis</em> 427, 115116 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcat.2023.115116">doi.org/10.1016/j.jcat.2023.115116</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Jaekwon Jeoung, Jonghyun Jeon, Jip Kim, Young Sun Mok, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Effects of dielectric particles on non-oxidative coupling of methane in a dielectric barrier discharge plasma reactor," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 377, 119896 (2019) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2018.09.057">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2018.09.057</a></li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Chemical Engineering, Seoul National University (1995)</li><li>M.S., Chemical Engineering, Seoul National University (1997)</li><li>Ph.D., Chemical Engineering, Seoul National University (2001)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Team Leader and Senior Researcher, LG Chem Research Park (2001–2009)</li><li>Principal Researcher, Korea Research Institute of Chemical Technology (KRICT) (2009–2014)</li><li>Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2014–present)</li><li>Research Group Leader, C1 Gas Refinery R&amp;D Center, Sogang University (2017–2024)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>Guest Editor, Chinese Journal of Catalysis (2023–2024)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Mansoor Ali, Muhammad Kashif Khan, Muhammad Zubair, Faisal Zafar, Sheraz Ahmed, Muhammad Asif, Ahmed Haleley, Zaman Sajid, Jong Wook Bae*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Integrated Framework for Electrochemical N₂ Reduction to NH₃: Mechanistic Pathways, Theoretical Descriptors, and Data-Driven Catalyst Design," <em>Carbon Energy</em> (2026), accepted</li><li>Seojin Shin, Kyeongjun Seo, Seung-Jun Baek, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Wangyun Won*, "Ethylene production from shale gas using a dielectric barrier discharge plasma reactor: an integrative circular economy perspective," <em>Green Chemistry</em> 28, 11764–11778 (2026) – Front Cover <a href="https://doi.org/10.1039/d5gc07016c">doi.org/10.1039/d5gc07016c</a></li><li>Minkyeong Ban, Juchan Kim, Hyeonae Im, Seongseop Kim, Hoang Phuong Nguyen, Yongju Yun, Jeong Woo Han*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Jinwoo Lee*, "Light oils from methane homologation over hierarchically porous TiO₂/SiO₂ hybrid catalyst for a non-thermal plasma," <em>Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy</em> 386, 126437 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126437">doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126437</a></li><li>Hyeonae Im, Hoang Phuong Nguyen, Yunkyung Kim, Juchan Kim, Chaesung Lim, Yongju Yun, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Jeong Woo Han*, "Computationally guided dopant discovery for boosting TiO₂ catalysts in plasma-assisted non-oxidative coupling of methane," <em>Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy</em> 383, 126051 (2026) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2025.126051">doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2025.126051</a></li><li>Dong Hyeon Kim, Hee Hwan Kim, Juchan Kim, Youngchang Byun*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Recovery of methyl methacrylate from waste poly(methyl methacrylate) pellets using a low-temperature plasma and zeolites," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 497, 154438 (2024) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.154438">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.154438</a></li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Ethylene Production Processes in a Carbon-Neutral Strategy," <em>Energy Conversion and Management</em> 311, 118462 (2024) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.enconman.2024.118462">doi.org/10.1016/j.enconman.2024.118462</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Seongseop Kim, Minkyeong Ban, Dongmin Lee, Seongbeen Kim, Jinwoo Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Unravelling the effects of short pore on Fischer-Tropsch synthesis and its role as selectivity controller," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 475, 146039 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.146039">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.146039</a></li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "A Combined Production Technology for Ethylene and Hydrogen with an Ethane Cracking Center and Dielectric Barrier Discharge Plasma Reactor," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 462, 142155 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.142155">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.142155</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Chaesung Lim, Dongmin Lee, Hayoung Jeong, Jeong Woo Han*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Effects of oxygen species in perovskite catalysts on the partial oxidation of methane in a low temperature plasma bed," <em>Journal of Catalysis</em> 427, 115116 (2023) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcat.2023.115116">doi.org/10.1016/j.jcat.2023.115116</a></li><li>Juchan Kim, Jaekwon Jeoung, Jonghyun Jeon, Jip Kim, Young Sun Mok, Kyoung-Su Ha*, "Effects of dielectric particles on non-oxidative coupling of methane in a dielectric barrier discharge plasma reactor," <em>Chemical Engineering Journal</em> 377, 119896 (2019) <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2018.09.057">doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2018.09.057</a></li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>저희 연구실은 가스로부터 고부가가치 화학물질을 생산하는 촉매 기술을 연구합니다. 메탄과 CO₂ 같은 온실가스, 그리고 제철소와 화학산업에서 나오는 배가스·부생가스는 중요하고 풍부한 반응 원료입니다. 대표적인 온실가스인 메탄은 직접 또는 간접 전환을 통해 올레핀, 방향족, 알코올, 합성연료, 전기 등 최종 제품으로 바뀔 수 있습니다.</p><p>비열 플라즈마 촉매를 이용한 메탄·CO₂ 직접 전환<br>저온·상압에서 작동하는 유전체 장벽 방전(DBD) 플라즈마 반응기에서 메탄을 활성화해 아세틸렌, 에틸렌, 에탄 같은 경질 탄화수소를 생산합니다. 비열 플라즈마 전환에 맞게 설계된 새로운 촉매를 개발해 온실가스를 올레핀, 경질유, 메탄올, 에탄올, 아세트산 등 고부가가치 제품으로 전환하는 것이 주된 목표입니다. 귀금속을 담지한 3차원 규칙 거대기공(3DOM) 촉매에서는 CH₄와 CO₂를 동시에 그린 메탄올과 아세트산으로 전환해 친환경 수송 연료와 저배출 단량체 합성에 활용할 수 있습니다. 현재는 CCS로 포집한 CO₂와 버려지는 CH₄로부터 의미 있는 전환율과 수율로 그린 메탄올을 얻기 위해, 새로운 촉매와 재생에너지 기반 비열 플라즈마 기술을 결합한 고선택성 촉매를 개발하고 있습니다.</p><p>C1 가스 간접 전환: GTL, 그린 메탄올과 지속가능 항공유(SAF)<br>C1 가스를 합성가스로 먼저 만든 뒤 후속 합성 단계를 거치는 간접 전환도 연구합니다. 대표 기술인 GTL(gas-to-liquids)은 개질 반응으로 합성가스(수소와 일산화탄소)를 만들고, 이어서 피셔–트롭시 합성이나 메탄올 합성을 수행합니다. 저희는 분산성과 환원 특성이 우수한 고규칙성 나노다공성 촉매를 개발하며, 이를 이용해 포집한 CO₂와 재생에너지로 만든 청정 H₂로부터 그린 메탄올과 지속가능 항공유(SAF)를 합성합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Our main focus is the catalytic production of valuable chemicals from gases. Greenhouse gases such as methane and CO₂, together with off-gases and byproduct gases from steelmaking and the chemical industry, are important and abundant reactants. Methane, a major greenhouse gas, can be converted directly or indirectly into final products such as olefins, aromatics, alcohols, synthetic fuels, and electricity.</p><p>Direct Conversion of Methane and CO₂ by Non-Thermal Plasma Catalysis<br>We activate methane in a dielectric barrier discharge (DBD) plasma bed, which operates at low temperature and ambient pressure, to produce light hydrocarbons such as acetylene, ethylene, and ethane. Our main objective is to develop new catalysts designed specifically for non-thermal plasma conversion, so that greenhouse gases can be turned into high-value products such as olefins, light oils, methanol, ethanol, and acetic acid. Over noble-metal-incorporated three-dimensionally ordered macroporous (3DOM) catalysts, CH₄ and CO₂ are converted simultaneously into green methanol and acetic acid for green transportation fuels and low-emission monomer synthesis. We are now developing unique, selective catalysts that achieve meaningful conversion and yield of green methanol from CCS-captured CO₂ and waste CH₄, combining new catalysts with non-thermal plasma powered by renewable energy.</p><p>Indirect Conversion of C1 Gases: Gas-to-Liquids, Green Methanol and SAF<br>We also study the indirect conversion of C1 gases, in which synthesis gas is generated first and then converted in one or more further synthesis steps. A key technology is gas-to-liquids (GTL): reforming first produces synthesis gas (hydrogen and carbon monoxide), which is then converted by Fischer–Tropsch or methanol synthesis. We develop highly ordered nanoporous catalysts with better dispersion and reduction properties, and use them to synthesize green methanol and sustainable aviation fuel (SAF) from captured CO₂ and clean H₂ produced from renewable energy.</p>$q$,
  lab_ko = $q$지속가능 탄소중립 연구실$q$,
  lab_en = $q$Carbon Neutral Laboratory for Sustainability$q$,
  lab_url = $q$https://sites.google.com/view/kshalab$q$,
  building = $q$R$q$,
  room = $q$515$q$,
  office = $q$리치과학관(R) 515호$q$,
  keywords = $q$Heterogeneous Catalysis, Ordered Nanoporous Materials, Non-thermal Plasma, C1, Greenhouse Gas, Fischer–Tropsch, Methanol$q$
where name_ko = '하경수';

select name_ko, lab_ko, lab_en, lab_url, office, keywords, length(bio_ko) bio_ko, length(bio_en) bio_en, length(research_ko) res_ko, length(research_en) res_en from faculty where name_ko = '하경수';
